{"id": "EUVD-2026-81813", "enisaUuid": "39080c73-2815-3ee3-9f6e-65fc55e36e0d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: seq: Don't leak the extension cell pointer in the bounce payload\n\nThe bounce_error_event() embeds the failed event in the bounce payload\nby pointing data.ext.ptr at it.  When that event is a queued\nvariable-length event, its own data.ext.ptr holds the address of its\nfirst extension cell, put there by snd_seq_event_dup().  The payload\ngoes out verbatim through snd_seq_expand_var_event(), so the address\nreaches userspace.\n\nThat is the same address commit 705dd6dcbc0e (\"ALSA: seq: Clear\nvariable event pointer on read\") removed from the event header.  The\nread path still clears it there, just above the call that expands the\npayload.\n\nEmbed a sanitised copy instead, treated exactly as snd_seq_read()\ntreats the header.  A stack copy is enough because delivery is\nsynchronous and snd_seq_event_dup() copies before returning.\n\nAn unprivileged client reaches this by setting SNDRV_SEQ_FILTER_BOUNCE,\nqueueing a variable-length event to a port that does not exist and\nreading the bounce back.  Eight bytes on 64-bit, from its own pool.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42c3f856d13a91a0d4c302a0c6854813621136db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b1e8d40663997aacaa198f37ce6893e07aaba77a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e6e471eef1d5d8cb056c7d364023fe048249204", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/59e1592d3c270ff4642d5d6dc55c545306eb0693"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90220", "GHSA-r7hx-2638-9jpm"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05cc2f32-d3bd-30be-8eaf-939daca3a634", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.160 <6.7"}, {"id": "08279713-ae0d-345c-b292-bd2cc75c76ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0527a56cb327021cb73167cfddf0e49efa043500"}, {"id": "17c5acd6-59a9-3304-96c6-d83add7eefdc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.97 <6.12.110"}, {"id": "27cafee9-e685-3dd8-8769-f8758136d3c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5e91991d-3f34-34d9-ba8e-2faa4f52c2e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "efc86691e4d8083d9e380ea95042c2cf679f65fd <59e1592d3c270ff4642d5d6dc55c545306eb0693"}, {"id": "6b94ea09-cc61-3f54-97b0-5f2e7c7a328d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "80e3d8d3-e0f5-3dc3-9320-90b30a2ff1d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "8523da5c-fc8f-3e2d-bf53-8d51d61a7243", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "93d260ce43a81df579c98bee92b91316df9c1c57 <42c3f856d13a91a0d4c302a0c6854813621136db"}, {"id": "879e1451-3886-3bd1-8e73-ec3882cb9698", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "8a73589a-cb44-3c62-8283-29e87dbb1a5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "efc86691e4d8083d9e380ea95042c2cf679f65fd <6e6e471eef1d5d8cb056c7d364023fe048249204"}, {"id": "ade915e3-4263-3b7c-a62b-dd79bfa1838f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.2"}, {"id": "b210c181-082b-3e4e-9c49-308d4c420e4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dae23c545eb5a2be3b27a82fd0f611894fb8ab69 <b1e8d40663997aacaa198f37ce6893e07aaba77a"}, {"id": "b7cf9fd8-7960-3502-aa5b-3043f34536d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "cdd271ed-cfaf-3cfb-a246-ce3552cdaa7a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "